  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe StakingManager contract has a critical issue with how withdrawal amounts are calculated and processed, which can lead to insufficient liquidity for later withdrawals after a slashing event. The root cause is that withdrawal amounts are calculated at the time of queueing rather than at confirmation time, which creates an unfair distribution of remaining funds after slashing.\n\n### Attack Path\n\nIgnoring the rewards for the simplier calculations\n\n- User1 and User2 both stake 100 HYPE tokens each, receiving 100 kHYPE tokens each.\n- Total HYPE in the system: 200 tokens\n- Total kHYPE supply: 200 tokens\n- Exchange rate: 1 kHYPE = 1 HYPE\n\nNow User1 queues a withdrawal of 100 kHYPE tokens:\n- Calculated HYPE to return: 100 HYPE tokens\n- This amount is stored in User1's withdrawal request\n\nA slashing event occurs, penalizing 60 HYPE tokens:\n- New total HYPE in the system: 140 tokens\n- Total kHYPE supply: 200 tokens (unchanged because user1's tokens are not burned yet) \n- New exchange rate: 1 kHYPE = 0.7 HYPE\n\nUser2 now queues a withdrawal of 100 kHYPE tokens:\n- Calculated HYPE to return: 70 HYPE tokens\n- This amount is stored in User2's withdrawal request\n\nAfter the withdrawal delay, User1 confirms and receives 100 HYPE tokens:\n- Remaining HYPE in the system: 40 tokens\n\nWhen User2 tries to confirm their withdrawal for 70 HYPE tokens:\n- Only 40 HYPE tokens remain in the contract\n- The transaction will revert due to insufficient balance\n\n### Impact\n\n1. Users who attempt to withdraw after slashing events may be unable to receive their funds.\n2. Unfair Distribution of Slashing Penalties\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nCalculate withdrawal amounts at confirmation time, not queue time",
  "proof_of_concept": "To run this test:\n\n1. Add this function to the `StakingManager.t.sol` test file\n2. Run the test with: `forge test --match-test test_InsufficientLiquidityAfterSlashing -vvvv`\n\nThe test shows that User1 can successfully withdraw their entire pre-slashing amount, but User2 cannot withdraw their funds because there is insufficient liquidity left in the contract.\n\n```solidity\nfunction test_InsufficientLiquidityAfterSlashing() public {\n        uint256 stakeAmount = 100 ether;\n        \n        // Setup validator and delegation\n        vm.startPrank(manager);\n        validatorManager.activateValidator(validator);\n        validatorManager.setDelegation(address(stakingManager), validator);\n        stakingManager.setMaxStakeAmount(0);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        // Create two users who will stake the same amount\n        address user1 = makeAddr(\"user1\");\n        address user2 = makeAddr(\"user2\");\n        \n        // Both users stake the same amount\n        vm.deal(user1, stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user1);\n        stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n        \n        vm.deal(user2, stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user2);\n        stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n        \n        // User1: queue withdrawal right before slashing(Time in between where oracleAdapter updates the slashing but oracleManager is not updated yet)\n        vm.prank(user1);\n        kHYPE.approve(address(stakingManager), stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user1);\n        stakingManager.queueWithdrawal(stakeAmount);\n\n        // Add ETH to the StakingManager contract to process both withdrawals\n        vm.deal(address(stakingManager), stakeAmount * 2);\n        \n        // User1 initial withdrawal amount before slashing\n        StakingManager.WithdrawalRequest memory user1Request = stakingManager.withdrawalRequests(user1, 0);\n        uint256 withdrawalAmountBefore = user1Request.hypeAmount;\n        \n        // Slashing happens Within the 7 days of withdrawal (30% of stake is slashed)\n        uint256 slashAmount = 60 ether; // 30% of total staked (200 ether)\n        vm.prank(address(oracleManager));\n        validatorManager.reportSlashingEvent(validator, slashAmount);\n\n        // User2 queues withdrawal after slashing\n        vm.prank(user2);\n        kHYPE.approve(address(stakingManager), stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user2);\n        stakingManager.queueWithdrawal(stakeAmount);\n        \n        // Fast forward to after the withdrawal delay\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + stakingManager.withdrawalDelay() + 1);\n        \n        // Both users confirm their withdrawals\n        vm.prank(user1);\n        stakingManager.confirmWithdrawal(0);\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + stakingManager.withdrawalDelay() + 1);\n        \n        // Save the withdrawal amount after slashing\n        StakingManager.WithdrawalRequest memory user2request = stakingManager.withdrawalRequests(user2, 0);\n        uint256 withdrawalAmountAfter = user2request.hypeAmount;\n        \n        vm.prank(user2);\n        stakingManager.confirmWithdrawal(0);\n        \n        // User1's withdrawal amount should be higher than User2's because User1 queued before slashing\n        assertGt(withdrawalAmountBefore, withdrawalAmountAfter, \"User1 should get more HYPE than User2\");\n        \n        // Verify that User1 effectively avoided the slashing penalty\n        console.log(\"User1 withdrawal amount\", withdrawalAmountBefore);\n        console.log(\"User2 expected withdrawal amount\", withdrawalAmountAfter);\n        console.log(\"Balance remain in the contract:\", 200e18 - slashAmount - withdrawalAmountBefore);\n    }\n```",
